  "description": "ZEPXOL crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 41/a c d. Reported CIF formula moiety: C224 H222 Dy12 N50 Na4 O84,10(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 6 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.643-4.791 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.11-149.34°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C224H222Dy12N50Na4O94. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
